// Simple IF statements
// Max Score: 2 | Difficulty: Not Specified
// For this challenge, write a program to take an integer as input, output what the number is, then check to see if the number is 10.

// If it is 10, display the message "It's a match".

// The expected input is:
// An integer
// e.g. 10
// The expected output is:
// "The number is 10"
// "It's a match"

// IF statements allow programmers to perform different blocks of code, depending on the current conditions/variable values inside of their programs.

// The basic pseudocode syntax is :

// IF <condition> THEN
//   // code to be executed
// END IF
// In Java, it will look like this :

// if(variable > 5){
//   System.out.println("The number is greater than 5");
// }
DECLARE values:INTEGER
INPUT values
OUTPUT "The number is",values
IF values=10 THEN
    OUTPUT "It's a match"   
ENDIF


